# Slate's threat model (SECURITY.md §1) names this file as the first
# mitigation: a contributor who edits only Markdown can put text into every
# future agent session's context window, and a docs-only diff is the kind
# reviewers skim. These paths get a named reviewer on every pull request.

# The context layer the agent is told to trust.
/.slate/            @gurbirdhaliwal
/AGENTS.md          @gurbirdhaliwal
/CLAUDE.md          @gurbirdhaliwal

# Agent wiring that executes on clone (SECURITY.md §2) and the write gates
# that decide what an agent may change (§3).
/.claude/           @gurbirdhaliwal
/.cursor/           @gurbirdhaliwal
/.mcp.json          @gurbirdhaliwal

# Supply chain: CI, the published action, and release/packaging metadata.
/.github/           @gurbirdhaliwal
/action.yml         @gurbirdhaliwal
/pyproject.toml     @gurbirdhaliwal
/.pre-commit-hooks.yaml @gurbirdhaliwal

# Security and licensing statements.
